  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Sylvester’s sequence is defined by the recurrence relation:\n$$a_{n+1}=1+(a_0\\times a_1\\times\\cdots\\times a_n)$$\nand $a_0=2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Determine the first five terms of this sequence.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2,\\ 3,\\ 7,\\ 43,\\ 1807$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a_0&=2\\\\a_1&=1+2=3\\\\a_2&=1+2\\times3=7\\\\a_3&=1+2\\times3\\times7=43\\\\a_4&=1+2\\times3\\times7\\times43=1807\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Prove that $a_{n+1}=a_n(a_n-1)+1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a_{n+1}=a_n(a_n-1)+1$.\n\nFor $n\\ge1$, substitute $a_0a_1\\cdots a_{n-1}=a_n-1$ into the defining recurrence; $n=0$ also holds.",
          "worked": "For $n\\ge1$, the defining recurrence gives $a_0a_1\\cdots a_{n-1}=a_n-1$. Hence,\n$$\\begin{align*}a_{n+1}&=1+a_0a_1\\cdots a_n\\\\a_{n+1}&=1+a_n(a_0a_1\\cdots a_{n-1})\\\\a_{n+1}&=a_n(a_n-1)+1.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $n=0$, $a_1=3=2(2-1)+1$, so the result also holds.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, prove that\n$$\\frac1{a_n}=\\frac1{a_n-1}-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac1{a_n-1}-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}=\\frac1{a_n}$.\n\nUse $a_{n+1}-1=a_n(a_n-1)$ and combine the fractions.",
          "worked": "From part (b), $a_{n+1}-1=a_n(a_n-1)$. Therefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{a_n-1}-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}&=\\frac1{a_n-1}-\\frac1{a_n(a_n-1)}\\\\\\frac1{a_n-1}-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}&=\\frac{a_n-1}{a_n(a_n-1)}\\\\\\frac1{a_n-1}-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}&=\\frac1{a_n}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Hence, prove that\n$$\\sum_{i=0}^{n}\\frac1{a_i}=1-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=0}^{n}\\frac1{a_i}=1-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}$.\n\nSum the identity in part (c); all intermediate terms cancel.",
          "worked": "Using part (c), the sum telescopes:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum_{i=0}^{n}\\frac1{a_i}&=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}\\left(\\frac1{a_i-1}-\\frac1{a_{i+1}-1}\\right)\\\\\\sum_{i=0}^{n}\\frac1{a_i}&=\\frac1{a_0-1}-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}\\\\\\sum_{i=0}^{n}\\frac1{a_i}&=1-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q13-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Hence, deduce that\n$$\\sum_{i=0}^{\\infty}\\frac1{a_i}=1.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$.\n\nAs $a_{n+1}\\to\\infty$, the remaining reciprocal term tends to zero.",
          "worked": "All terms are integers at least $2$, and part (b) gives\n$$a_{n+1}-a_n=(a_n-1)^2\\ge1.$$\nThus $a_{n+1}\\to\\infty$. Taking the limit in part (d),\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum_{i=0}^{\\infty}\\frac1{a_i}&=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left(1-\\frac1{a_{n+1}-1}\\right)\\\\\\sum_{i=0}^{\\infty}\\frac1{a_i}&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
